2result.sql correctly limits the analysis to wholesale items (by intersecting veg_loss_rate_df with veg_whsle_df), computes the mean and true population variance (hence standard‑deviation band), and then classifies every SKU into below / within / above ±1 σ before aggregating the counts.  
0result.sql and 1result.sql ignore the veg_whsle_df filter, so they summarise all loss‑rate records rather than only wholesale items, making their results out‑of‑scope.

